        },
        {
            "presentation_step_number": "2",
            "title": "Agent Diversity & Architectures",
            "narration_statement": "But not all agents work the same way. There are different types built on different architectures designed for different kinds of problems. And understanding those differences is what allows you to match the right agent to the right job.",
            "matching_section": "Purpose: Explain Agent Diversity & Architectures in Solara & Lesson Objectives\nDominant Visual: Visual metaphor for agent diversity and problem matching.\nVisual Choreography: Below the Solara flow, a dynamic visual appears: Three distinct, stylized 'Agent' icons (e.g., a simple gear, a compass, a multi-faceted diamond) orbit a central 'Problem Sphere'. Each agent icon is labeled [Type 1], [Type 2], [Type 3]. Animated lines connect each agent to the Problem Sphere, with the line to the 'right' agent for the problem glowing, suggesting 'matching'. Problem Sphere pulses, changing internal patterns to represent 'different problems'.\nPersistence: Clean anchor across steps."
        },
        {
            "presentation_step_number": "3",
            "title": "Learning Outcomes",
            "narration_statement": "By the end of this topic, you will be able to describe the core components that make up an AI agent's architecture. Explain how agents interact with their environment through a continuous loop. Walk through the perception reasoning action cycle that drives agent decision making and identify the three main types of agents and one each as appropriate, as well as visualize how a complete agent workflow flows from input to outcome.",
            "matching_section": "Purpose: Explain Learning Outcomes in Solara & Lesson Objectives\nDominant Visual: Progressive reveal of learning objectives as key bullet points.\nVisual Choreography: A series of concise objective statements animate onto the screen sequentially, each accompanied by a small, relevant icon (e.g., building blocks for 'components', a circular arrow for 'loop', a brain for 'cycle', three distinct shapes for 'types', a flowing arrow for 'workflow'). Each objective appears slightly below the previous one. Titles remain concise. All elements below y=1.6.\nPersistence: Clean anchor across steps."
        }
